    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "the question",
      "script_lines": [
        "L02",
        "L03"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Teams make decisions in meetings, emails and tickets. Months later, someone asks: why did we decide this, who approved it, and is it still true? The answer is scattered across documents, and some are out of date.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17.1,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B01_Scattered"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 12.65,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 12.666666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B01_Scattered",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "what it does",
      "script_lines": [
        "L04",
        "L05"
      ],
      "narration_text": "DecisionTrace Lite answers them: a short answer, the decision's current status, and a citation to the exact passage behind every claim. If the documents don't say, it says so instead of guessing.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 14.8,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B02_AnswerCard"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 12.5,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 12.5,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B02_AnswerCard",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "why it matters",
      "script_lines": [
        "L06",
        "L07"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Why it matters: a wrong answer about a decision looks exactly like a right one, and acting on a reversed or unfinished decision means redoing work. An answer you can check in seconds is one a team can rely on. And I'll publish how often it's right.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 21.7,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B03_WhyItMatters"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 15.55,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 15.583333333333334,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B03_WhyItMatters",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "existing tools",
      "script_lines": [
        "L08",
        "L09"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Here's what already exists. General tools like NotebookLM and ChatGPT answer questions about documents you upload, and point to where an answer came from.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.1,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B04_Tools"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 10.22,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 10.25,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B04_Tools",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "research",
      "script_lines": [
        "L11"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Research laid the groundwork. Retrieval-augmented generation, from Lewis and colleagues in 2020, grounds answers in retrieved text. The ALCE benchmark measures whether citations support their sentences. RAGAS scores how faithful an answer is to its sources.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 16.6,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B05_Research"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 17.24,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 17.25,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B05_Research",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "my test",
      "script_lines": [
        "L13"
      ],
      "narration_text": "So I tested two tools myself. On October ninth, I gave NotebookLM and ChatGPT six synthetic documents about a fictional company switching databases. The switch was approved, but not finished.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13.8,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B06_TestSetup"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 13.55,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 13.583333333333334,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B06_TestSetup",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "notebooklm",
      "script_lines": [
        "L14"
      ],
      "narration_text": "NotebookLM got the facts right and refused to invent a budget. But it described the migration as if it were done.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 9.7,
      "shot": {
        "type": "STILL",
        "motion": "hold",
        "treatment": "none"
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 7.19,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
