      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "act": "the gap",
      "script_lines": [
        "L16",
        "L17"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Neither tool told me how often it's right. That's the gap. Existing tools find facts. DecisionTrace Lite is built around a decision's status. It checks every citation, and it publishes its score.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 14.8,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B09_Gap"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 12.67,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 12.708333333333334,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B09_Gap",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "act": "larger system",
      "script_lines": [
        "L18",
        "L19"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Here's the plan, step by step. This is a scoped-down version of a larger system I've built, with Neo4j, LangGraph, FastAPI and hallucination detection. Here I keep only the core: question in, grounded answer out, in plain Python with Claude.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 18.5,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B10_LargerToLite"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 16.73,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 16.75,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B10_LargerToLite",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "act": "data",
      "script_lines": [
        "L20"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Step one: data. I'll grow my six synthetic Northwind Logistics documents into about fifty meeting notes, emails and tickets. Some decisions get reversed, some are unfinished, some documents contradict each other, and some questions have no answer. All of it is synthetic.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 19.4,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B11_Data"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 17.37,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 17.375,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B11.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B11_Data",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B12",
      "act": "test set",
      "script_lines": [
        "L21"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Step two: about fifty test questions I write by hand, each with the correct answer, status and supporting passages. I write them myself because Claude helps generate the documents, and a model grading its own homework isn't a test.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 18.0,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B12_TestSet"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 14.42,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B12.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 14.458333333333334,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B12.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B12_TestSet",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B13",
      "act": "retrieve + answer",
      "script_lines": [
        "L22",
        "L23"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Step three: retrieval. A simple keyword ranker called BM25, written with Python's standard library, finds the most relevant passages. Step four: Claude returns structured JSON: an answer, a status, and a list of claims, each with a document ID and an exact quote.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 19.8,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B13_RetrieveAnswer"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 18.11,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B13.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 18.125,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B13.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B13_RetrieveAnswer",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B14",
      "act": "verify",
      "script_lines": [
        "L24",
        "L25"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Step five: verification. Code checks that every quote appears word for word in its document, and a second Claude call judges whether the quote supports the claim. An answer that fails gets one retry. If it still fails, the tool says: not supported by the sources. Step six: the evaluation harness and a written report.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 25.4,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B14_VerifyLoop"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 20.54,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B14.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 20.541666666666668,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B14.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B14_VerifyLoop",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B15",
      "act": "resources",
      "script_lines": [
        "L26"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Resources. Claude runs through my Northeastern Claude Code seat, in non-interactive mode. Using it from a script is pending confirmation from my professor and Northeastern IT. If it isn't allowed, I'll request API credits instead. Saved responses let me re-score without new calls. Compute is my M4 MacBook Pro, with no GPU, plus GitHub for the code.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 26.3,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B15_Resources"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 23.51,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B15.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 23.541666666666668,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B15.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B15_Resources",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B16",
      "act": "five measures",
      "script_lines": [
        "L27",
        "L28",
        "L29",
        "L30",
        "L31"
      ],
      "narration_text": "How will I know it worked? Along with basic correctness, I'll measure five things on my test set. One: citation validity. Every quote must exist in the cited document. Target: one hundred percent. Anything less is a bug. Two: citation support. Does each quote actually support its claim? Target: at least ninety percent. Three: status accuracy. Decided, in progress, or superseded? Target: at least eighty-five percent. Four: refusals. It should refuse at least nine in ten unanswerable questions, and no more than one in ten answerable ones.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 40.2,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B16_Measures"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 36.88,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B16.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 36.916666666666664,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B16.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B16_Measures",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B17",
      "act": "worked or not",
      "script_lines": [
        "L32",
        "L33"
      ],
      "narration_text": "Five: does the verifier help? I'll compare the full tool against the same tool with verification off. It worked if it meets those targets, and the verifier improves support and status accuracy without costing more than five points of correctness. It didn't work if verification only adds refusals, or if the second Claude call disagrees with my own judgments too often to trust. Either way, I'll publish the numbers and the failures.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 33.2,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B17_Decision"
        }
      },
      "actual_duration_s": 25.43,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B17.mp3",
      "render_duration_s": 25.458333333333332,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B17.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B17_Decision",
        "at": "2026-11-22T13:38:07"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B18",
      "act": "first check",
      "script_lines": [
        "L34"
      ],
      "narration_text": "The first check: asked which database the tracking service uses, it has to say the switch is still in progress as of June ninth, citing the migration ticket. Those are the two things the other tools missed.",
      "voice": "af_heart",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "estimated_duration_s": 17.1,
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
